From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rk808: add -clkout names to rk8xx_clk_id_table

The MFD driver (drivers/mfd/rk808.c) registers subdevice cells named
e.g. "rk817-clkout", "rk805-clkout", "rk816-clkout", etc.
Because rk808_clkout_driver specifies an id_table, platform bus matching
only compares against id_table entries. The id_table only had entries
without "out" ("rk817-clk"), causing probe failure and preventing
clocks (such as <&rk817 1>) from being registered.

Add the corresponding -clkout names to rk8xx_clk_id_table.

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c
@@ -202,10 +202,16 @@ static int rk808_clkout_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct platform_device_id rk8xx_clk_id_table[] = {
 	{ "rk805-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk805-clkout", 0 },
+	{ "rk808-clkout", 0 },
 	{ "rk809-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk809-clkout", 0 },
 	{ "rk816-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk816-clkout", 0 },
 	{ "rk817-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk817-clkout", 0 },
 	{ "rk818-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk818-clkout", 0 },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(platform, rk8xx_clk_id_table);
